  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Twelve kilometres of brine channel cut into the salt crust with working floors alongside, operated from 2258 until the crust failed in a series of collapses in 2295. Around a thousand people worked it at its height. The cuts are still open, drifting slowly full of ochre dust, and the toppled boundary markers along the eastern side are the best-dated objects on the planet.</p>",
